      "text": "Tissue culture allows any piece of plant tissue — a leaf disc, a shoot tip, an embryo — to regenerate into a complete plant under sterile laboratory conditions. This capability, called totipotency, is the biological foundation for a technology that produces hundreds of millions of plants annually."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
