        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE MICROPROPAGATION PIPELINE:"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md#004",
      "path": [
        "03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:horticulture:03-tissue-culture, git-history:horticulture:03-tissue-culture]",
        "canonical_path": "horticulture/03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[tissue, culture]",
        "current_path": "horticulture/03-TISSUE-CULTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:horticulture:tissue-culture",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "horticulture",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[tissue, culture]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tissue Culture and Micropropagation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXPLANT SELECTION\n  (piece of donor plant)\n        |\n        v\n  SURFACE STERILIZATION\n  (eliminate microorganisms)\n        |\n        v\n  Stage I: ESTABLISHMENT        Culture initiated in sterile medium\n  (weeks to months)              Explant establishes; contamination eliminated\n        |\n        v\n  Stage II: MULTIPLICATION       Shoot proliferation stimulated by cytokinin\n  (continuous, months)            Each cycle: 3–10× multiplication of shoots\n        |\n        v\n  Stage III: ROOTING             Auxin applied; roots induced\n  (weeks)                         Plants become self-sufficient\n        |\n        v\n  ACCLIMATIZATION                Transition from controlled lab to nursery\n  (weeks)                         The critical bottleneck\n        |\n        v\n  TRANSPLANT-READY PLANTLET\n```"
    },
    {
